ProjectALife = ProjectALife or {}
ProjectALife.DialogueShards = ProjectALife.DialogueShards or {}
ProjectALife.DialogueShards["radio_10"] = {
{"r4_sad_cat_on_truck_hood","caller_story_sad",9,30,5,10,1,{"Caller - Harlan","Morning, this is early, I know, I've been up since before light watching a cat","Marty","A cat, Harlan","Caller - Harlan","My son-in-law drove a milk route, left the house at five-thirty every morning, he'd start the truck and let it warm up ten minutes while he finished his coffee","Caller - Harlan","That barn cat figured it out years back, five-thirty, she's up on the hood, soaking up the engine - every morning, rain or shine","Caller - Harlan","Truck hasn't started in two weeks, nobody left to start it - it's summer, the metal's cold at that hour anyhow","Caller - Harlan","Five-thirty this morning she's up on that hood - sitting, waiting on it to get warm","Caller - Harlan","I went out and put my hand on the hood next to her - she let me, she doesn't let anybody","Dee","(Dee doesn't answer, there's the sound of her setting a cup down, carefully)","Caller - Harlan","Well, I'll let y'all go"}},
{"r4_sad_friday_pancake_letters","caller_story_sad",9,30,6,11,1,{"Caller - Denise","I want to tell you about breakfast on Friday - the ninth, if that's alright, nothing happens in it","Dee","Those are the good ones - go ahead","Caller - Denise","Pancakes, my husband made them in the shape of letters, because it was Friday and he was off - J for Jenna, T for Tyler","Caller - Denise","Tyler's T came out looking like a hammer, and he wouldn't eat it till it was fixed - so Rick cut a piece off it with the spatula","Caller - Denise","The window was open because it was already hot, the neighbor was mowing - the kitchen smelled like cut grass and syrup","Caller - Denise","Rick flicked water on the griddle to see if it was ready and it spit at him and he cussed and the kids told on him","Caller - Denise","That was about seven-thirty - Friday, seven-thirty in the morning, Friday the ninth","Dee","(Dee lets the quiet hold for a long time)"}},
{"r4_sad_curfew_eleven","caller_story_sad",9,30,20,23,1,{"Caller - Brent","Thursday night my daughter asked to stay out till one - she's sixteen, there was a thing at the lake - I said eleven","Caller - Brent","She said all her friends' parents said one, I said then all her friends can come home at one - she can come home at eleven","Caller - Brent","She said she hated me, she slammed her door so hard the picture fell off the hall wall - and Friday morning she was gone to her friend's before I got up","Marty","Kids say that","Caller - Brent","I know they do, and I was right, is the thing - Eleven's right, those lake parties aren't any place for sixteen","Caller - Brent","I've thought about it every way, I'd say eleven again - I would","Caller - Brent","I just wish I'd hung that picture back up before she came home - so it wasn't still on the floor, so it wasn't the last thing in the hall","Dee","(Dee lets out a breath, she doesn't say anything)","Caller - Brent","It's still on the floor, I can't pick it up now - sorry - go on to the next one"}},
{"r4_sad_siphon_stranger","caller_story_sad",9,30,12,21,1,{"Caller - Tanya","I've got to tell somebody about a man, I don't know his name - nobody's ever going to know his name","Dee","Go ahead, hon","Caller - Tanya","Tuesday I ran out of gas on the Irvington road with three kids in the back seat - just rolled to a stop, middle of nowhere","Caller - Tanya","A pickup came up behind me, older man, feed cap, big belly, I thought, here we go, this is how it happens","Caller - Tanya","He didn't say a word, got a hose out of his truck bed and siphoned his own tank into my car - spit gas in the ditch twice","Caller - Tanya","When he was done he looked in at the kids and said, y'all be good for your mama - and he got his rifle and a sack out of the truck","Caller - Tanya","And he started walking - north - toward Louisville, his truck just sitting there empty in the road with the door open","Caller - Tanya","He gave me all of it, he didn't keep enough to get anywhere himself - I looked back in the mirror and he didn't even look back","Marty","(Marty clears his throat, and then again)","Dee","Feed cap, big belly, walking north, if anybody sees him, somebody on the Irvington road says thank you"}},
{"r4_sad_timer_six_oclock","caller_story_sad",9,30,17,20,1,{"Caller - Earlene","It's almost six, I have to set down the phone - the mic, I have to set it down for a second at six","Dee","Take your time, Earlene","Caller - Earlene","There, that was the kitchen timer, the wind-up kind, shaped like a chicken - it doesn't need a battery","Caller - Earlene","Six o'clock was Harold's insulin, twenty-two years I set that chicken so he wouldn't forget - he forgot anyway, I'd have to holler","Caller - Earlene","There's no insulin left, there's no Harold - I know that","Caller - Earlene","I still wind it at five every day and let it ring at six - I stand in the kitchen and let it ring all the way out","Caller - Earlene","And I holler - Harold, it's six - Harold - it's six","Caller - Earlene","I don't care who hears me holler - that's all","Dee","(Dee says nothing, the chicken timer rattles to a stop somewhere on the caller's end)"}},
{"r4_sad_rita_bike_tube","caller_story_sad",9,30,9,18,1,{"Marty","Knox County Radio, ninety-nine six, you're on the air","Caller - Rita","Hi, we lost my husband and his daddy at the checkpoint in Muldraugh on the tenth - so it's me and the boys now","Caller - Rita","Anyway - does anybody have an inner tube for a kid's bike? Twenty inch - the boys have been fighting over the one bike that works","Dee","Twenty inch - okay","Caller - Rita","I can trade a jar of peanut butter, it's opened, but only once","Marty","(A pause - Marty starts to say something about the checkpoint, and Dee touches his arm, and he stops)","Dee","Twenty-inch bike tube, opened peanut butter, anybody out there, call in","Caller - Rita","Thank you, they'll be so happy - they're good boys, I'll get off now"}},
{"r4_sad_hospice_ice_chips","caller_story_sad",9,30,20,23,1,{"Caller - Wanda","Dee, you're a nurse - can I ask you a nurse question? It's after the fact - it doesn't matter now","Dee","Ask me anything, Wanda","Caller - Wanda","My mother had the cancer, she was at home on hospice, the nurse came Tuesdays and Fridays - the last one didn't come","Caller - Wanda","At the end she couldn't swallow, she wanted ice chips, but the power was out - there was no ice anywhere","Caller - Wanda","I wet a washrag with well water and let her suck on the corner - she kept asking for ice, she kept saying, it's warm, honey","Caller - Wanda","Was that alright? Was the washrag alright? That's my whole question","Dee","Wanda, that is what I would have done - that is exactly what we do when there's no ice - the washrag was right","Caller - Wanda","Thank you... I just needed somebody who'd know","Dee","(Dee keys the microphone twice and doesn't speak either time)"}},
{"r5_host_dee_first_night","host",9,11,0,23,4,{"Marty","There's somebody sitting across the desk from me tonight, and I'd like her to say hello before she thinks better of it","Dee","Hi - I'm Dee, I worked nights as a nurse in Muldraugh for eleven years, so I'm used to being awake when nobody sensible is","Marty","Deanna came by to trade me a box of gauze for dog food and ended up rewrapping my hand instead","Dee","He'd tied a cut shut with feed sack string, feed sack string, everybody, on the radio he sounds like he knows things","Marty","I never claimed to know things, I claimed to have a transmitter","Dee","Well, now you've got a nurse, if you're hurt and you can reach this station, I'll talk you through what I can","Dee","I can't come to you, I need that to be real clear - but I can talk a person through a lot","Marty","She means it, she's already talked me out of two bad ideas tonight","Dee","Three, you didn't tell them about the ladder"}},
{"r5_trade_rules_first","trade",9,30,9,17,3,{"Marty","We're going to try something my father listened to every weekday on the AM out of Elizabethtown - a swap show, we'll call ours the Trading Post","Marty","Three items a caller - tell us what you've got, what you want, and a place out in the open where you'll meet - daylight only","Marty","No guns and no ammunition traded on this station, I know you need them - I won't be the voice that sent somebody to get shot over a box of shells","Dee","And no medicine unless I've heard what it is first - I already heard a man trying to pass off horse wormer as antibiotics","Marty","It did not come from my store, before anybody asks","Dee","It absolutely came from his store, the price sticker says Colburn Feed","Marty","Bring one person to the trade and leave another watching from a distance - alright, the Trading Post is open"}},
{"r7_ksp_last_one_on_the_parkway","scanner",9,14,0,6,1,{"Trooper 418","Post 4, 418 - radio check","Trooper 418","Post 4, 418, anybody at the post, key up","Trooper 418","This is Kentucky State Police unit 418, if there's any unit on this channel, any unit at all, key your microphone","Trooper 418","All right, I'm sitting at milepost 94 westbound, which is where I've spent most of my working life","Trooper 418","There's no cars on this road, not stopped, not wrecked, not nothing, cleanest I have ever seen this parkway","Trooper 418","I'm going to run it one time to the county line and one time back, and then I'm going home to Cecilia. 418, out"}},
{"r8_hor_clocks_at_ten_after","caller_story_horror",9,120,1,5,1,{"Verna","I want to say four ten, ten after four - I'd say four ten","June","Start at the front of it for me","Verna","House on Halbert, mine, I mean, it's my aunt's, I been staying in it since the water quit","Verna","She's got clocks, nine of 'em, kitchen clock, the mantel one, the wind-up in the hall, a cuckoo thing that never worked","Verna","They're all set to the same time now - all nine, the wind-up too, and that one needs a key, and I got the key in my apron","June","Are you in that house right now?","Verna","I'm in the garage with the mower and the door down - I ain't going back in there tonight","June","Stay in the garage, I'm going to stay on this line a while","Verna","Thank you, hon, you don't have to talk - just don't hang it up"}},
{"r8_hor_chalk_numbers_doors","caller_story_horror",9,110,23,5,2,{"Sudie","Somebody's chalked a number on every front door on Halbert Street","June","What kind of numbers?","Sudie","Ones and twos, mostly, a three on the corner house, little numbers, down low by the knob, so you got to be looking","Sudie","My door's got a two on it, I live by myself","June","You live alone and the door says two","Sudie","Two, and the Tandy house, that's a family of five, has got a one on it","June","So it isn't people","Sudie","I don't know what it's counting and I washed mine off with a rag and a bucket","Sudie","It was back Wednesday, same corner of the door - two"}},
{"r8_hor_notebook_rewritten","caller_story_horror",9,110,22,4,1,{"Pauline","I keep a notebook, spiral one, the little one, what we ate, what we used, who's sick","June","A log","Pauline","My daddy kept one on the farm his whole life so I keep one - it sits on the windowsill by the sink","Pauline","Tuesday's page is wrote out again, same words, in my hand, on the next blank page","June","In your handwriting","Pauline","Mine, I know my own hand, and I didn't do it, and I've never once in my life wrote a page twice","June","Is anybody else in the house?","Pauline","My husband can't write, that's not a secret, he'll tell you himself - and the boy's four","Pauline","I'm keeping the notebook on me now, in my apron, that's the only change I've made"}},
{"r8_hor_music_in_the_trees","caller_story_horror",9,110,23,5,1,{"Reba","Somebody's got a little music going out in the woods behind our place - faint, like a wind-up thing","June","Can you make out what it is?","Reba","No, it's too far and there's not enough of it - three notes and then it's gone and then three notes","Reba","Here's the part that keeps me up, it quits when the wind quits","June","Then the wind's carrying it","Reba","That's what a sensible person says, and I said it first - but the wind carries a sound, it don't switch it off","Reba","When the wind drops there ain't nothing - not quieter - nothing, and then the wind comes up and it's right there again","June","You follow that?","Reba","I do and I wish I didn't, my husband says leave it alone, so we're leaving it alone"}},
{"r8_hor_dog_in_the_chimney","caller_story_horror",9,110,1,5,1,{"Hazel","There's a dog barking in my chimney","June","In the chimney","Hazel","Down in the flue, behind the damper. Big stone chimney, old house. We shut it off years ago","Hazel","My husband took a light up on the roof. No bird's nest, no coon. He even put his arm down in there","June","And it kept on?","Hazel","It quit while he was up there, started back before he had the ladder down","June","Does it sound like a dog you know?","Hazel","Yes. Roscoe. That's what I didn't want to say. Roscoe's been dead since April","Hazel","We're sleeping in the back bedroom now. That's... that's all I know to tell you"}},
{"r8_hor_half_second_late","caller_story_horror",9,110,22,4,1,{"Estill","There's a way to say this that don't sound crazy and I ain't found it, so I'm just going to say it","June","Say it however it comes","Estill","Fella we took in for two nights, you'd ask him something and he'd answer a half second late","June","Slow to answer","Estill","Not slow, that's what I keep trying to get across - Slow's a man thinking, this was the same gap every time","Estill","Same gap, like there was somebody in between us, passing it along","June","What did he answer with?","Estill","Right answers, every one - somebody said pass the salt and he passed it, half a second late","Estill","We give him breakfast and pointed him at the road - I ain't proud of it and I'd do it again"}},
{"r8_hor_back_to_the_door","caller_story_horror",9,115,23,5,1,{"Hoyt","We had a man overnight, seemed like a hand, you know, seemed like somebody who'd be useful","June","Go on","Hoyt","He sat with his back to the door all night","June","Nobody does that now","Hoyt","Nobody does that, there's twelve of us and every one of us sits where we can see a door, and nobody taught us that, we just do it","Hoyt","He put his chair square against the door and faced the room - faced us","June","Watching the room","Hoyt","Watching the room, and whichever way you cut it, either he's got nothing to be afraid of out there, or he ain't afraid of what's out there","Hoyt","I took the chair out of that room, my wife thinks I've lost my mind and she may be right"}},
{"r8_hor_flag_up_blank_paper","caller_story_horror",9,115,22,4,1,{"Hazel","Mailbox flag's up every morning - mine, out at the end of the drive","June","Somebody putting mail in?","Hazel","A piece of paper, folded in three, the way you'd fold a letter for an envelope - every morning, nine days","June","What does it say?","Hazel","Nothing - it's blank, both sides, and I hold it up to the sun and I've held one over a candle, which my husband says is how you burn a house down","June","Nine blank pages","Hazel","Same paper, too, lined tablet paper, the wide kind, off the same tablet - you can see where they've been tore out","June","Have you left one of your own?","Hazel","No, somebody said do that, put a note in there and ask what they want - I ain't going to be the one that answers it"}},
{"r8_hor_hour_on_the_overpass","caller_story_horror",9,110,23,5,1,{"Imogene","My husband drove a truck, long haul, thirty-one years - he's gone, that's not what this is about","June","All right","Imogene","I went up on the overpass north of Muldraugh Saturday - I don't know why, to look at the road, I guess","Imogene","I sat up there an hour and nothing went by","June","There's not much moving","Imogene","An hour - both directions, I know it was an hour, I had his watch","Imogene","The road was dry and clear and open all the way to the curve, and nothing come and nothing went","June","That's a lot of quiet to sit in","Imogene","Here's what I'll say and then I'm getting off, that road never once was empty - not in thirty-one years, not at three in the morning on Christmas"}},
{"r8_hor_deer_wont_move","caller_story_horror",9,115,21,3,1,{"Doyle","Three deer standing in the middle of the Ekron road at noon","June","At noon","Doyle","Broad daylight, two does and a yearling, right in the wheel tracks, facing up the road, away from me","Doyle","I laid on the horn - nothing, rolled up to twenty foot and blew it again, and I mean blew it","June","They didn't run","Doyle","Not a flick of an ear, a deer'll come out of its skin at a gravel crunch - these stood there like cows at a gate","June","What did you do?","Doyle","I sat, ten minutes maybe, then they walked off into the beans on the left, all three together, at a walk","Doyle","They was looking up the road the whole time, and I turned around and went home the long way, and I ain't been up that road since"}},
{"r8_sad_machine_greeting","caller_story_sad",9,120,22,4,2,{"June","Go ahead, you're on ninety-nine six","Opal","Our answering machine still had her on it, the greeting, I mean, the little outgoing part","June","Your wife?","Opal","You've reached the Tandys, we can't get to the phone, leave a message and we'll call you back - thirty-one words, I counted 'em one night","June","And you've been playing it","Opal","Batteries in the thing, it's got a little cord but there's no juice in the wall, so it's the batteries","Opal","I ran 'em flat, I knew I was doing it while I was doing it, too - sat there in that kitchen and ran 'em flat","June","How many times?","Opal","I don't know, it got fainter and slower and then it was just the little light, and then the light went too","Opal","If anybody's got two of them square nine volts, I'd trade a good hatchet - that's really why I called and it took me eleven minutes to get to it"}},
{"exp_matching_buttons","caller_story_sad",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Lottie","My mother kept spare buttons in a cookie tin","June","Were there ever actual cookies in it?","Lottie","Not in my lifetime, I checked every visit anyway","June","An optimistic child","Lottie","An optimistic forty-year-old, near the end","Lottie","I lost a coat button yesterday and knew exactly who I wanted to ask","June","That's a hard little moment","Lottie","I'm leaving the button missing for now"}},
{"exp_guest_towels","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Lottie","We had towels nobody was allowed to use","June","For guests, I assume?","Lottie","The guests weren't allowed either, those towels were above all of us","June","A purely decorative authority","Lottie","Mother would put them out and then watch everybody's hands","June","Did anybody ever manage to use one?","Lottie","My cousin, we still talked about it at holidays","June","Every family needs a scandal it can survive"}},
{"exp_mystery_label","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Bess","Found a can with the label half peeled off","June","Did the other half offer any clues?","Bess","Said family favorite, which narrows it down to everything nobody likes","June","You don't have to risk dinner on a slogan","Bess","I'm saving it for when I need an occasion","June","An occasion for what?","Bess","Being disappointed in a family I've never met","June","Food criticism remains alive and unnecessarily personal"}},
{"exp_inventory_husband","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Frances","My husband could never find anything in the pantry","June","Even when it was in front of him?","Frances","Especially if it was in front of him, that was its best hiding place","June","Did you have to look for him?","Frances","I'd describe the shelf like I was landing an airplane","June","And that worked?","Frances","Eventually, he'd say somebody must have moved it","June","A very small household conspiracy"}},
{"exp_unknown_knocking","caller_story_horror",10,3650,21,5,1,{"Morris","There were three knocks, that part I remember clearly","June","Are you talking about something happening now?","Morris","No, days ago - somewhere I already left","June","Alright, I don't want listeners mistaking this for a call for help","Morris","I asked who it was, didn't get a name","June","Did the knocking continue?","Morris","No, that's why I still think about it","Morris","Wish I knew whether somebody was waiting for my courage or my stupidity"}},
{"exp_clock_tick","caller_story_sad",10,3650,22,5,1,{"Edith","The kitchen clock used to sound enormous when the house was asleep","June","I remember clocks like that","Edith","I thought silence would be peaceful, never understood how much that ticking was doing","June","Keeping you company?","Edith","Making tomorrow sound inevitable","June","That's a lot of work for a kitchen clock","Edith","Cheap one, too, crooked plastic numbers","June","Didn't need to be expensive to earn its place"}},
{"exp_club_minutes","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Red","Our president still wants somebody to take meeting minutes","Duke","Because otherwise you remember whatever suits you","Red","We're arguing over cans of peaches, history can live without the record","Duke","You said that when you owed dues, too","Red","Was hoping the end of everything might clear my account","Duke","Treasurer had very neat handwriting, we can still read it","Red","This is why I never trusted an organized man","Duke","Put that objection in the minutes"}},
{"exp_chopshop_clock","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Harlan","I knew a fellow who could take a car apart faster than he could explain owning it","June","I'm sensing we're near the edge of a story I shouldn't ask questions about","Harlan","He was hopeless with the clock on the dashboard","June","That does sound like a safer subject","Harlan","Could identify an engine by ear, couldn't set eleven-thirty","June","Everybody has a limit","Harlan","His whole life ran six hours behind","June","Perhaps that explains his difficulty accounting for where he'd been"}},
{"exp_postal_address","caller_story_sad",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Celia","I sorted mail by the sound of the names in my head","June","You knew that many people?","Celia","Knew their envelopes, who got birthday cards, who only got bills","June","That's a particular way of knowing a town","Celia","I liked the thick letters, somebody had made time for those","Celia","Now I've got things I want to say and nowhere to put a stamp","June","You can say some of them here","Celia","I'd rather the right person heard, but thank you"}},
{"exp_barn_echo","caller_story_horror",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Silas","A tobacco barn talks all night if you let yourself listen","June","Wood settling, that sort of thing?","Silas","Wood, loose tin, something small moving under the floor","Silas","I grew up with those noises, knew every one","June","Do they bother you now?","Silas","It's the ones that stop when I move","June","Have you found what's making them?","Silas","Sometimes a mouse, sometimes nothing where I look"}},
{"more_radio_front_steps","caller_story_sad",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Wade","I built my mother's front steps too high","June","When was this?","Wade","Years back, she told everyone they were perfect","Wade","Showed the neighbors - 'look what Wade did for me'","Wade","Then I'd see her going sideways to get down them","June","Did you change them?","Wade","I said I would, kept saying it","June","I'm sorry, Wade","Wade","Don't know why I'm telling strangers about steps","June","I don't mind listening - go on, if you want"}},
{"more_radio_crook_safe","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Harlan","A man once tried to sell me a safe he couldn't open","Harlan","Says there's valuables inside, I ask how he knows, 'well, look at it'","Harlan","Look at WHAT? It's shut, that's our whole problem","Caller","You buy it?","Harlan","Eventually, used it to prop a door open","Caller","Ever open it?","Harlan","Three summers later, combination was inside, on a little card","Caller","You're making that up","Harlan","Why would I tell it like that if I was lying? I'd put money in the damn thing","Harlan","Still got it, as far as I know, holding that same door"}},
{"more_radio_not_a_confession","caller_story_sad",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Harlan","I gave somebody back a watch once","June","You'd bought it?","Harlan","Bought it? Uh... no, let's leave that part alone","Harlan","Had a name scratched on the back - a date","June","You found the owner?","Harlan","He found me, showed me the pale mark on his wrist","Harlan","I charged him nothing, that's the part people don't believe","Harlan","He kept asking what I wanted for it, I said, take the watch - just take it","June","Did he?","Harlan","Yeah, looked back twice walking away, can't say I blame him"}},
{"king_radio_tomato_argument","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Ed","My wife says I used to talk too much about tomatoes","June","Did you?","Ed","There's no short answer to that","June","I think there might be","Ed","You sound just like her","June","She sounds sensible","Ed","She wants me to mention she was listening","June","Hello, Ed's wife. Thank you for your patience"}},
{"king_radio_haircut","caller_joke",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Sheila","I let my husband cut my hair","June","How'd he do?","Sheila","I'm going to need him to remain behind me for the rest of our marriage","June","That bad?","Sheila","He keeps saying it'll grow","June","Hard to argue with","Sheila","Oh, I'm managing","June","Tell him to quit while you've still got some"}},
{"king_radio_fathers_knife","caller_story_sad",10,3650,0,23,1,{"Cal","Dad gave me a pocketknife when I was twelve. Made me give it back in a week","June","What happened?","Cal","Carved my name into his good chair","June","That'll do it","Cal","Years later he gave it back. Didn't mention the chair","June","You still have it?","Cal","Yeah. Haven't carved a damn thing","June","He might've been pleased to hear that"}},
{"r2_d10_man_with_a_well","military",10,14,19,2,1,{"Farmhouse","Any soldier on this net who's tired of standing on a road for nothing - this is a former sergeant of the line, we have a farm, a well, a wall, and room for six more with rifles","Warden Tac","Unknown station, you are transmitting on a military net, identify yourself, over","Farmhouse","I identified myself for eleven years, now I'm a man with a well, boots and rifles are welcome - officers are not","Warden-6","This is Warden-6, any soldier who leaves his post to join that man will be charged with desertion, over","Farmhouse","Colonel, respectfully - who exactly is going to convene the court?","Warden-6","The United States Army, over","Farmhouse","Then tell them to come on in and get us - they'll have to get through your checkpoints first - farmhouse, out"}},
{"r3_so_d10_shift_report","sign_on",10,14,5,7,1,{"Dee","Good morning, this is Dee, finishing up the overnight - Marty's in the back looking for his other boot","Dee","Overnight was quiet on the scanner, one trucker came on nineteen wanting to argue about basketball, so I let him, because he sounded lonely and he was wrong","Marty","Morning, I heard some of that, he was wrong","Dee","Report for day shift, two folks at the back door with cuts, both clean, both bandaged - one lady with sugar diabetes, out of insulin, I don't have any - I told her so","Dee","If anybody has insulin, keep it as cool as you can and bring it to the feed store - it will not go to waste, that's all from me - I'm going to go lie down on the seed sacks","Marty","It's {time}, ninety-nine point six, and the day shift is on"}},
{"r3_sf_d10_shoes_by_bed","sign_off",10,20,22,23,1,{"Marty","That'll do it for today, before I go: count your people, check your locks, and put your shoes where you can find them in the dark","Marty","Shoes, because if you have to run in the night, you don't want to be doing it in your sock feet on gravel - Dee has seen what that looks like","Dee","I have - shoes","Marty","Ninety-nine point six is going off the air - good night"}},
{"r3_host_d10_pen_line","host",10,20,9,20,1,{"Caller - Terry","Breaker one-nine for the nurse lady, this is Terry, up by the rock quarry","Dee","Go ahead, Terry, this is Dee","Caller - Terry","My wife cut her hand on a can lid Tuesday - it's all swelled up, and there's a red streak going up her arm about to the elbow","Dee","Okay - Terry, that's infection moving up the arm, and it's serious - does she have a fever?","Caller - Terry","She's hot, she says she's fine","Dee","She's not fine - warm soaks, clean cloth, hot as she can stand it, four times a day - keep that arm up above her heart, and Terry, take a pen and draw a line on her arm where the red stops","Dee","If the red's past your line by morning, she needs an antibiotic - go through every medicine cabinet you can get into, and bring me anything ending in cillin or mycin","Caller - Terry","Pen line - okay, thank you, ma'am","Dee","And Terry, you tell her the nurse said she's not fine - let her be mad at me instead of you"}},
{"r3_host_d10_at_this_time","host",10,30,0,23,1,{"Dee","Can I say something about how Marty talks on the radio?","Marty","You're going to anyway","Dee","The first week, he said 'at this time' in front of everything - 'at this time, boil your water.' 'At this time, the scanner is quiet'","Marty","I got that from the Emergency Broadcast System, I figured they knew how to talk to people","Dee","Honey, they were a long beep and a man reading a card","Marty","At this time, I'd like Dee to go back to bed","Dee","See? He's getting better"}},
{"r3_ins_d10_bucket_and_lime","instruction",10,30,0,23,1,{"Dee","Nobody wants to hear a nurse talk about toilets on the radio - tough","Dee","If your toilet doesn't flush, quit using it - use a bucket with a lid, and throw a scoop of lime or dirt or wood ashes in after every use - Marty has lime","Marty","I have a great deal of lime","Dee","If you dig a latrine, dig it at least two hundred feet from any well or creek, and downhill from them - not uphill - downhill","Dee","And wash your hands after, with soap, I don't care that the world ended, the germs have never been happier"}},
{"r3_wx_d10_heat_lightning","weather",10,20,5,10,1,{"Marty","Several of you asked about the flashes over the knobs last night with no thunder - that was heat lightning, a storm too far off to hear - it isn't shelling, and it isn't anything the Army's doing","Marty","I only mention the Army because six of you asked","Marty","Today, ninety-one and sticky, and that storm over the knobs might wander our way by evening - might not","Marty","If it does, it'll come on fast - get the laundry in - get the kids in - get the lids off the rain barrels"}},
{"r3_mb_d10_clock_radio","music_bridge",10,30,0,4,1,{"Dee","On nights, the nurses' station had a clock radio that only pulled in one station, and after midnight it only played slow ones","Dee","We said it was the radio's way of telling the residents to go back to sleep - it never worked on them, it worked on us","Dee","I don't have that radio, so this is the part of the night where you'd hear a slow one - close your eyes for three minutes, I'll watch the door"}},
{"r4_sad_dee_three_am_light","caller_story_sad",10,30,2,5,1,{"Dee","Marty's asleep in the chair, it's just me, somebody asked earlier what I miss about nights at work, and I lied and said the coffee","Dee","We had a resident at the home before I went to the clinic - Mr. Rucker - ninety-one, sharp as a tack in the daytime","Dee","Every night, three o'clock, his call light went on - every night, I'd go down the hall and he'd say, what time is it, nurse?","Dee","I'd say three o'clock, Mr. Rucker, he'd say, that's what I thought, and he'd go back to sleep, seven years he did that","Dee","He passed in the spring, nothing to do with any of this - just ninety-one","Dee","I still wake up at three, every night since the power went - no clock in here, but I know","Dee","And I say it, out loud, to nobody, three o'clock, Mr. Rucker","Dee","(Dee sits back from the microphone, a long quiet)","Dee","That's what I thought"}},
{"r4_sad_brother_wes_reunion","caller_story_sad",10,30,18,23,2,{"Caller - Dana","I'm looking for my brother - Wesley Burke - Wes, he drove a tow truck in West Point - last I heard he was going to the bridge","Dee","Wes Burke - tow truck - West Point, anybody who knows Wes Burke, get on the air","Caller - Dana","He's got a tattoo of a bass on his arm - it's a terrible tattoo, it looks like a shoe","Marty","We've got another caller coming in - go ahead","Caller - Wes","Dana?","Caller - Dana","(A sound on the line that isn't a word)","Caller - Wes","Dana, it's a bass, it is a bass - I've told you it's a bass","Caller - Dana","I'm sitting down, I'm on the kitchen floor - I don't know how I got on the floor","Caller - Wes","I'm at the fire station in Riverside, there's eight of us - where are you? No, don't say it on the radio - Dee, can she give you her road off air?","Dee","She can - stay right there, both of you - don't neither of you move","Marty","(Marty takes his headphones off and sets them on the desk - for almost a minute, no one on the station says anything at all)"}},
{"r5_host_dee_radio_voice","host",10,45,0,23,1,{"Dee","Can I say something about Marty's radio voice?","Marty","I'd rather you didn't","Dee","With the microphone off he talks like any man in March Ridge - the second he presses that button, he's reading the evening news in nineteen fifty-eight","Marty","My father listened to the farm report at noon every day of his life - those men had voices, somebody ought to carry it on","Dee","He says good evening when nobody's called in for an hour - to nobody, I've watched him do it","Marty","Somebody might be listening who can't press the button, you don't know","Dee","That's fair, good evening, whoever can't press the button"}},
{"r5_joke_extension_pamphlets","caller_joke",10,60,17,22,1,{"Marty","We've got Deborah on the line from Rosewood - go ahead, Deborah","Caller - Deborah","Marty, you know the county extension office by the courthouse?","Marty","I do, I've sat through their pasture management talk - twice","Caller - Deborah","They've still got a sign in the window - 'is your family prepared for a disaster? Free pamphlet inside'","Marty","Did you go in?","Caller - Deborah","I went in, they're all out of pamphlets","Caller - Deborah","So somebody's family is real prepared, I guess"}},
{"r5_obit_caller_wilma_mail","obituary",10,60,8,20,1,{"Marty","Go ahead, caller, you're on ninety-nine point six","Caller - Tina","I want to say something for Wilma Shotts, she carried the rural route out of Ekron for twenty-two years","Caller - Tina","If your mama lived three boxes down, Wilma would carry a dozen eggs from you to her - never charged, said the government didn't need to know about eggs","Marty","I knew Wilma, she'd tap the horn going past my loading dock every day at eleven-fifteen","Caller - Tina","On the ninth she finished the route - every box, nobody knows how, with what was going on that day","Caller - Tina","I had a piece of mail from her in my box - the last one she ever put in","Caller - Tina","It was my water bill, I've still got it - I haven't opened it"}},
{"r5_joke_floyd_shed_roof","caller_joke",10,90,17,22,1,{"Caller - Floyd","Marty, I got up on my shed roof to get away from three of them yesterday","Marty","Good thinking, Floyd","Caller - Floyd","They wandered off in about ten minutes","Marty","So you got down","Caller - Floyd","No sir, I'm fifty-eight - turns out getting up on a roof is something you do on fear, and getting down is something you do on a ladder","Caller - Floyd","Which I had kicked over, on the way up, also on fear","Marty","How'd you get down, Floyd?","Caller - Floyd","My wife - around supper, she stood there a good long while first, just looking at me"}},
{"r7_ksp_post4_closes","scanner",10,16,5,11,1,{"Post 4","All units, this is Post 4, as of {time} this post is not manned - this is the last scheduled broadcast from this radio room","Post 4","The generator's got about six hours in it, when it quits, the repeater on the hill quits, and car to car is all you'll have","Post 4","There's a key to the post in the light fixture by the back door and there's forty-one gallons of water in the basement","Post 4","The wall map's got everything I know marked on it in grease pencil - roads that are closed, houses that answered, houses that didn't","Post 4","Any unit still in a car is released to go home to their families - that is a direct order from the post commander and I'll write it out and sign it","Trooper 406","Post 4, 406 - who's going to sit at that desk?","Post 4","I am, 406, till it quits, then I'm going to lock the door out of habit and walk to Cecilia - post 4, clear"}},
{"r8_hor_white_towel_barn","caller_story_horror",10,120,23,4,1,{"Junior","Barn out behind the Kelso place - you know it? Out past where the pavement quits","June","I'll take your word for it","Junior","Whole barn's rot and flies - Roof's half gone, hay in there's been wet since spring, smells like a hog lot","Junior","And there's a white towel hung on a nail by the door - folded - dry","Junior","Dry, June, in that barn, I put my hand on it","June","Why did you touch it?","Junior","'Cause I'm stupid, I guess, it was clean - it was clean like it come off a line","Junior","So that's why we don't go past the Kelso place no more - don't go past it"}},
{"r8_hor_hymnal_same_page","caller_story_horror",10,120,22,3,1,{"Estill","Cedar Grove Methodist, little Bethel's cousin church, out the county road","June","I know where you mean","Estill","We went in for the kitchen, they got a big kitchen - went in the sanctuary first 'cause the side door was chained - no, hold on, front door was chained - we went in the side","Estill","Every hymnal in every pew is laid open - same page, twenty-two pews, both sides","June","The same page in all of them","Estill","Same page, I checked nine or ten of 'em before I quit checking - I ain't telling you the number of the page","June","You don't have to","Estill","I ain't telling it - ask Earl Kemble, he was stood right there next to me - he'll tell you what it was"}},
{"r8_hor_truck_mile_markers","caller_story_horror",10,120,23,4,1,{"Rex","Brown pickup on 31W, parked on the shoulder, nose south, hood down","June","Abandoned?","Rex","That's what I took it for - Monday it was about even with the creek - Tuesday it was up past the church by a good half mile","Rex","Wednesday it was past the big curve, same truck, same dent in the tailgate, same nose south","June","Somebody's driving it","Rex","Then they're driving it half a mile a day, I ain't ever seen it move and I'm on that road every day of my life","June","I'd stay off that shoulder","Rex","I do now, I go by it in the far lane and I don't look in the cab - I looked in the cab one time and that's enough for me"}},
{"r8_hor_tire_tracks_mud","caller_story_horror",10,125,23,4,1,{"Orville","Mud hole at the bottom of our lane, it never dries, there's a spring under it, always has been","June","Go on","Orville","Tracks through it every morning, narrow tires, skinny ones, not a truck's, a car's","Orville","Going up the lane - toward us, never coming out","June","There's no other way out?","Orville","Dead ends at our barn, always has, forty acres and the one lane in and out","June","Then I'd want a look in that barn in the daylight, with people","Orville","We looked, four of us, Wednesday, ain't a car in that barn and ain't a track on that barn floor","Orville","So that's where I'm at, I'd rather it was in the barn, honest to God"}},
{"r8_hor_ball_no_shot","caller_story_horror",10,120,22,4,1,{"Imogene","There's a basketball goal at the end of Halbert Street - pole in the ground, no net on it for years","June","Somebody playing?","Imogene","Somebody dribbling - that's all, you hear a ball going on that concrete for an hour at a time","Imogene","Never a shot, that's what I'm calling about - a ball off a rim, off the backboard, you'd hear it, there's nothing quieter around here","June","Just the bouncing","Imogene","Steady, like a man thinking, and then it quits all at once, not slowing down like a ball does","June","Have you looked?","Imogene","From my window, there's nobody on that pad - I watched the whole time it was going and there was nobody on that pad","Imogene","I ain't telling the kids, they'd want to go see, I told 'em the water's off down that end of the street"}},
{"r8_hor_never_blinked","caller_story_horror",10,120,23,4,2,{"June","Go ahead, you're on","Burl","Fella sat at our fire Tuesday night - talked normal, ate his beans, said thank you, asked about the road north","June","So a traveler","Burl","Two, three a week come through - this one was nice enough, said his name was Walter, come up from Ekron","Burl","He didn't blink","June","Not once?","Burl","Hour and a half, I was across the fire from him and I got to watching, and then I couldn't quit watching","Burl","Everybody else went to bed, I set up till he left, he thanked me again at the gate - real polite","Burl","And then it got light out and we went on about our day - that's all that happened, I just don't want him back"}},
{"r8_hor_held_the_water","caller_story_horror",10,125,23,5,1,{"Glenda","A fella asked me for water, it was ninety-some degrees and he'd been walking, or he said he had","June","And you gave it to him","Glenda","Jar of it, cold, out of the springhouse - he said thank you, ma'am, and he held it","Glenda","Two hours he sat on that wall and held that jar - both hands, didn't drink a swallow of it","June","Maybe he was saving it","Glenda","That's what I said to myself, man's saving it for the road, that's a sensible thing and I said it to myself about nine times","Glenda","Then he set the jar on the wall, full, and walked off up the road","June","He left the water","Glenda","Left it full, I poured it out - I couldn't put that jar back in the springhouse and I couldn't tell you why"}},
{"r8_hor_no_mosquitoes_on_him","caller_story_horror",10,130,22,4,1,{"Alma","I'll tell you the whole silly thing - it's mosquitoes","June","There's plenty to go around","Alma","Ain't there, my boy's got forty bites on one arm - we sit out there slapping ourselves like a barn dance","Alma","This man sat two hours and never once swatted, not a twitch - hands on his knees the whole time","June","Some people don't get bit","Alma","They get bit, they just don't swell - but a mosquito on your neck, you brush it, you can't help yourself","June","So you watched his hands","Alma","Two hours, I know how that sounds, I sat and watched a stranger's hands not move for two hours","Alma","He said he'd be back through, so I've got that to think about - he said it real pleasant, too, the way you'd say it to a neighbor"}},
{"r8_hor_lot_facing_school","caller_story_horror",10,125,0,4,2,{"Loyd","Forty of 'em, maybe, in the lot at the school in Riverside - might be thirty, I'd say forty","June","That many in one place","Loyd","I've seen worse, that ain't it","Loyd","They wasn't making a sound, not one of 'em, you know that noise they make, that low one, in the chest","June","Nothing","Loyd","Nothing, forty people stood in a parking lot in the dark and not a sound out of 'em - you could hear the flag chain on the pole","June","Were they moving?","Loyd","Stood there, all of 'em facing the school - not the road, not me, and I had a light on - facing the building","Loyd","I backed the truck out with the engine off, rolled her down that hill in neutral - took four minutes and it took a year off me"}},
{"r8_hor_starlings_off_the_river","caller_story_horror",10,125,21,3,1,{"Almon","Field full of starlings on the bottom ground by the river - Thousands, you know how they cover a field","June","I do","Almon","They went up all at once, which they do, something spooks 'em, a hawk, a shot","Almon","They went away from the river","June","And that's wrong","Almon","Birds go to water, in this heat they'd go to the water and they went the other way, every one of 'em, and kept going","Almon","I stood there with a hoe in my hand and watched 'em go clean out of sight south","June","Did they come back?","Almon","Not that evening, not the next, and I'll say the rest of it flat, there's things in the river now and I know that, everybody knows that","Almon","But there's been things in that river three weeks and the birds never minded till Tuesday"}},
{"r8_hor_the_road_was_moving","caller_story_horror",10,130,0,4,3,{"Dee","Dee, ninety-nine six, you're up","Rex","You can see a piece of the highway up by Valley Station off the top of the water tower - the straight part, where it comes out of the trees","Dee","You climbed it?","Rex","For the view - that's all, I wanted to look at something besides this town","Rex","The road was moving","Dee","Vehicles?","Rex","No, the road was, the whole width of it, both lanes and the shoulders, going south, slow, like water in a ditch","Dee","How far could you see?","Rex","Far as the trees, mile, mile and a half - and all of it moving the same way at the same speed, and it was still moving when I come down","Dee","How long were you up there?","Rex","About forty minutes, then I got down and I told the man at the bottom it was cars - I lied to him and I'd lie to him again"}},
{"r8_sad_dog_at_ten_of_four","caller_story_sad",10,130,17,22,2,{"Marty","Evening, you're on ninety-nine six, go ahead","Hoyt","My brother's dog is at my place now, big red hound, name of Blue, which was my brother's idea of funny","Marty","How's he settling in?","Hoyt","Fine, eats, sleeps on the porch, good with my kids","Hoyt","Every afternoon at ten of four he walks down to the end of the lane and sits","Marty","Ten of four","Hoyt","My brother come off shift at the plant and went by that lane at ten of four for sixteen years - dog's got it to the minute","Marty","How long does he sit?","Hoyt","Till about dark, then he comes back up and gets in his spot and don't make a fuss about it","Hoyt","I've tried feeding him at quarter till to break it up - he eats and then he goes on down there anyway","Hoyt","Anyway, that's a dog - I don't know what I expected anybody to do about it - thanks for letting me say it out loud"}},
{"r9_host_d10_found_column","host",10,35,0,23,1,{"Marty","The corkboard by the register has got two sides now - one side says LOOKING FOR, the other side says FOUND, the FOUND side is a lot shorter and I mean to do something about that","Marty","Found, and every one of these is sitting in a coffee can on my counter - a set of keys with a rabbit's foot on the ring - a man's wedding band out of the Sav Rite lot, reading glasses in a hard blue case","Dee","And a child's shoe - one shoe, left foot, red, about a size seven","Marty","I'm not going to describe that one on the air again - if it's yours you already know what it is, you come here and knock and I'll hand it to you at the door","Marty","Nothing in that can gets traded, not for food, not for gas, not by me - it belongs to somebody"}},
{"r9_joke_d10_wife_hid_the_coffee","caller_joke",10,50,16,22,1,{"Caller - Orval","Marty, I need a neutral party","Marty","I'm a feed store, Orval","Caller - Orval","My wife has hid the coffee, there is a pound and a half of coffee in this house and I have not laid eyes on it since Sunday","Marty","She's rationing it","Caller - Orval","She's rationing me, there's a difference and she knows good and well there is","Marty","What does she say about it?","Caller - Orval","She says when I can name one thing I did today that wasn't complaining, I get a cup","Marty","And what did you tell her?","Caller - Orval","I told her I'd call the radio and get a ruling - she said, well, that's something, and poured me half a cup","Marty","There's your ruling - go to bed, Orval"}},
{"king_radio_instruction_book","caller_joke",11,3650,0,23,1,{"Evelyn","I've been reading a washing machine manual","June","Planning a repair?","Evelyn","No. Just nice when somebody tells you what the problem might be","June","Any luck with yours?","Evelyn","Apparently I should check the hose","June","Doesn't sound like the worst place to start","Evelyn","I'll let you know if it fixes the rest of my life","June","Please do. People would be interested"}},
{"r2_d11_precautionary","military",11,16,21,4,1,{"Keystone-3","Inside station calling for water, this is Keystone-3, on the outside of the line - I hear you, I can't reach you, over","Hatchet-2-3","Keystone-3, Hatchet-2-3, I know you can't, it's just nice hearing a voice that isn't scared, over","Keystone-3","I'm plenty scared, I'm just scared from farther away - where you from, over?","Hatchet-2-3","Paducah - you, over?","Keystone-3","Evansville - practically neighbors, same river, over","Hatchet-2-3","What's it like out there, over?","Keystone-3","Normal - too normal, my mom mailed me cookies and a newspaper, the paper says Knox County is under a precautionary quarantine, over","Hatchet-2-3","Precautionary - read me that word again, over","Keystone-3","Precautionary, over","Hatchet-2-3","That's a real good word - read it to me again some night - Hatchet-2-3, out"}},
{"r3_sf_d11_night_rounds","sign_off",11,25,0,2,1,{"Dee","Somebody on nineteen asked me to sing their little girl to sleep","Dee","I'm not going to, because I love you, and I've heard myself sing","Dee","What I'll do is tell her what the night nurse says on rounds - ready? Everybody on this hall is tucked in, the doors are locked - I'm walking up and down all night, nobody has to be awake but me","Dee","That's all there is to it, it worked on eighty-year-olds, it'll work on a five-year-old","Dee","Good night, ninety-nine point six is off the air"}},
{"r3_ins_d11_the_dead_near_home","instruction",11,30,0,23,1,{"Marty","This is a hard one, and I'm going to say it the way the county extension agent would have said it about livestock, because that's the only way I know how","Marty","If there are bodies near your house, they have to be dealt with - the heat's making it worse every day, flies, rats, dogs, and sickness getting into your well","Marty","Burying is best, deep, three feet of dirt on top at least, and well away from any water - if you can't dig, you can burn, but a body doesn't burn easy, and that smoke will be seen for miles","Marty","Wear gloves, tie a wet rag over your nose and mouth, do it at first light, while it's coolest","Marty","And if it's somebody you knew, write their name on something and leave it there - it doesn't take long, you'll be glad of it later"}},
}
